{"items":[{"id":"Structural coverage of capsid–receptor–glycan complexes","distance":"SAME","distance_reason":"Directly asks the binding-signatures half of the root: which capsid–receptor signatures can be computed rather than measured per complex.","scores":[{"criterion":"stakes","value":5,"reason":"Deciding whether to compute structural priors or run per-complex experiments turns on this; either answer redirects synthesis and assay budget."},{"criterion":"open","value":5,"reason":"Names model runs per pH; published work stops at 5 models/20 recycles and one measured pair; validation above that is unmeasured within reach."},{"criterion":"reshape","value":3,"reason":"Names 10^9–10^12-step chain and replica-decorrelation condition, but one replica fills a GPU and adaptive sampling already runs ensembles in parallel."}]},{"id":"Sequence-to-function ML on binding and transcytosis labels","distance":"ADJACENT","distance_reason":"Shares subject (AAV variants, transcytosis prediction) but asks whether a classifier can be accurate, not whether receptor-binding mapping determines fate.","scores":[{"criterion":"stakes","value":4,"reason":"Whether more transcytosis labels reduce false positives would steer label collection and whether classifiers, not binding maps, get built."},{"criterion":"open","value":5,"reason":"Names training-set size; published work stops at 24K variants with liver-targeting labels; effect of transcytosis labels above that unmeasured and cheaply reachable."},{"criterion":"reshape","value":1,"reason":"No sequential chain: trait models, seeds and replicates already fit independently in parallel with no step waiting on another."}]},{"id":"In-silico search of the capsid insert space","distance":"ADJACENT","distance_reason":"Same subject of AAV capsid design, but asks whether insert candidates can be enumerated in silico, not whether binding signatures determine transcytosis.","scores":[{"criterion":"stakes","value":1,"reason":"Already published: 10M variants scored to yield 88.4% multi-trait library; answer is settled and nothing turns on it now."},{"criterion":"open","value":1,"reason":"Settled within reach — published work already covers parallel scoring at 10M variants and showed its effect on design yield."},{"criterion":"reshape","value":1,"reason":"Every candidate is scored independently; no step waits on an earlier one, so only trivial sweep parallelism exists."}]},{"id":"Stochastic simulation of post-endocytic sorting","distance":"SAME","distance_reason":"Asks the transcytose-versus-intracellular half of the root question, targeting the sorting step that decides each variant's fate.","scores":[{"criterion":"stakes","value":5,"reason":"If sorting simulations predict real fate labels, effort shifts from binding mapping to compartment models; failure would redirect both approaches."},{"criterion":"open","value":5,"reason":"Names ensemble members per parameter point; published work stops at many independent sims with std devs; predicting real labels above that unmeasured, cheaply reachable."},{"criterion":"reshape","value":3,"reason":"Names event chain, GPU-idle realizations and decorrelation check, but the cited source already computes independent realizations in parallel for this system."}]}
